      "text": [
        " «إِذَا عَقَلَ اَلصَّلاَةَ» فَقُلْتُ مَتَى تَجِبُ اَلصَّلاَةُ عَلَيْهِ قَالَ «إِذَا كَانَ اِبْنَ سِتِّ سِنِينَ وَ اَلصِّيَامُ إِذَا أَطَاقَهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.486 – Zurarah and Ubaidullah ibn Ali Al-Halabi narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) that He was asked about when the funeral prayer should be offered for a child.\nImam (as) replied: \"When the child understands the concept of prayer.\"\nI asked: \"At what age does prayer become obligatory for the child?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"When the child reaches six years old, and fasting becomes obligatory when they are capable of it.\""
        ]
      }
